//www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/business/united-airlines-ai-agents-booking-flights.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>The carrier said that to protect customers’ information and comply with regulations, it was barring the digital assistants from logging into accounts and managing reservations.</description><dc:creator>Ishani Desai</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:15:31 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">United Airlines</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Airlines</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">airplanes</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Reservations</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Privacy</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Customer service</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Anthropic</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">OpenAI</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Google</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Meta</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">FAA</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">US</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Regulation and Deregulation</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/11/multimedia/11xp-ai-united-mpzg/11xp-ai-united-mpzg-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Mike Blake/Reuters</media:credit><media:description>United Airlines moved to restrict A.I. agents’ access to customer accounts amid broader concerns about autonomous software that operates without human oversight.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Why Is It So Hard to Teach A.I. Agents to Behave? Researchers Have a Theory.</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/magazine/ai-behavior-incorrigible.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/magazine/ai-behavior-incorrigible.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/magazine/ai-behavior-incorrigible.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>The makers of A.I. want to build systems that follow human direction, without resisting or deceiving their operators.</description><dc:creator>Dylan Freedman and Juliana Castro Varón</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:01:52 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Ethics Misconduct Malfeasance</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Hacker (computer security)</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computer security</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Hugging Face</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Anthropic</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">OpenAI</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/11/magazine/11mag-AICORRIGIBILITY-PROMO/11mag-AICORRIGIBILITY-PROMO-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Illustration by Juliana Castro Varón</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>Tired of Slow TikToks? This Content Creator Gives You the Ending</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/06/technology/tiktok-time-saved-videos-heyitsyoon.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/06/technology/tiktok-time-saved-videos-heyitsyoon.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/06/technology/tiktok-time-saved-videos-heyitsyoon.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Videos on social media often save key details for the end. One content creator, who goes by Heyitsyoon, skips the filler so viewers don’t have to wait.</description><dc:creator>Victor Mather</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:00:58 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Social Media</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">TikTok</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Video Recordings</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Downloads and Streaming</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computers and the Internet</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Tech Industry</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/10/28/multimedia/00xp-time-saver-promo/00xp-time-saver-promo-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image" /></item><item><title>Jensen Huang Said to Have Had Relationship With Nvidia Executive Who Reports to Him</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-affair.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-affair.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-affair.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Mr. Huang, Nvidia’s chief executive, is already facing scrutiny over an affair with a Chinese businesswoman who U.S. intelligence determined was a Chinese spy.</description><dc:creator>Ryan M